# Facebook Page or Profile for Earning (AI Niche): Full Growth Plan 2026

As of 24 October 2026. Niche used throughout: sharing AI tools, news, tutorials and workflows. Earnings are never guaranteed; this plan shows how to qualify and what Meta rewards.

---

## 1. Quick answer: Page or profile?

**Use a Facebook Page as your main earning asset.** Keep a personal profile (ideally in Professional Mode) as a supporting channel if you want to be the face of the brand.

| | Facebook Page | Profile in Professional Mode | Normal personal profile |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Can be monetized? | Yes | Yes | **No** (Meta says standard profiles are ineligible) |
| Best for | A topic brand ("AI tools and workflows") | A person-led brand | Friends and family only |
| Scheduling, analytics, team roles | Full (Meta Business Suite) | Professional Dashboard, fewer team options | None |
| Can be sold, handed over or shared | Yes, via roles | No (tied to you) | No |
| Risk | New Page starts with zero history | Mixing personal and public life | Cannot earn |

**Why a Page wins for AI content:** it is a brand you can scale, schedule, hand to an editor and later sell. Choose Professional Mode on a profile only if your face and name are the product (for example "Ali explains AI").

**Sources:** Meta's [Partner Monetisation Policies](https://www.facebook.com/business/help/169845596919485) say monetisation is available for public content on Pages, profiles in professional mode, Events and Groups, and not for ordinary profiles.

