## 3. Choose the AI niche angle (what "something new" means)

Do not post generic "top 10 AI tools" lists that everyone copies. Pick one angle you can make original:

| Angle | Example | Why it works |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tool tests | "I tested 3 free AI video tools for one week" | Your own proof, easy to repeat |
| Workflows | "How I make a weekly report in 4 minutes with AI" | Practical and saveable |
| AI for a profession | AI for teachers, shop owners, freelancers, students | Clear viewer, loyal niche |
| Before/after | Manual task vs AI-assisted task, timed | Strong hook, visual |
| Myths and mistakes | "5 AI prompts that waste your time" | Shareable opinions |
| News with analysis | What a new AI release means for normal people | Allowed only with your own analysis |
| Local language | AI tips in Urdu, Hindi, Arabic or Spanish for your audience | Less competition |

**Niche test (score 1-5, keep 16+):** Interest, Demand, Money path, Your edge.

**Rules that keep an AI Page safe**
- Show real screen recordings of tools you actually used. Do not repost other people's demos.
- Do not post fake or misleading AI content (fake news, fake celebrity endorsements, deepfakes of real people).
- Label realistic AI-generated or altered media; Meta adds "AI info" labels to AI content ([Meta transparency](https://transparency.meta.com/governance/tracking-impact/labeling-ai-content)).
- Use licensed music (Meta Sound Collection or tracks you have rights to).
- Do not make guaranteed-income claims ("earn $500 a day with this AI").

