## 5. Topic finding and research

**Where to find ideas (use 3+)**
1. Your own tool tests (the best source, and original).
2. Questions in Facebook Groups about AI, ChatGPT-style assistants, image and video tools.
3. Comments on competitor Pages ("how do I do this?").
4. Search bar suggestions on Facebook and Google Trends for AI topics.
5. Official release notes and blogs of AI tools (read, then test yourself).
6. Reddit and X communities for emerging tools.

**Research workflow**
1. Collect 30 ideas.
2. Search each topic on Facebook Reels; note view counts, post dates and gaps.
3. Find outliers (small Pages with big Reels) and study the hook, not the video itself.
4. Decide your original angle: your test, your numbers, your result.
5. Verify facts from the tool's official source before posting.
6. Score the idea (Demand, Gap, Edge, Hook strength, Effort), then schedule the top ones.

**Content mix**

| Type | Share | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reels (30-90 s) | 50-60% | Reach and earnings |
| Longer videos (3+ min) | 10-15% | Depth and trust |
| Photo/carousel/text posts | 20-30% | Cheap, also pays in Content Monetization |
| Stories and polls | daily | Audience touchpoints |

