## 6. Script guide (Reels and longer video)

**Reel structure (30-60 s)**

| Time | Job | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0-3 s | Hook that stops the scroll | "This free AI tool did my 2-hour task in 4 minutes." |
| 3-10 s | Context and promise | "I tested it so you do not have to. Here is the result." |
| 10-45 s | Show the steps on screen | Screen recording with short captions |
| 45-55 s | Result and proof | Before/after, timer, final output |
| Last 5 s | One CTA | "Want the prompt? Comment AI and I will send it." |

**Hook formulas:** result first; "stop doing X"; tool vs tool; time challenge; common mistake; secret setting.

**Rules:** one idea per Reel; cut the intro; change visual every 2-4 seconds; add on-screen text; end with a payoff or a loop so people replay.

**Script template**
```
TOPIC / VIEWER:
HOOK (0-3s):
PROMISE (3-10s):
STEPS (10-45s): step 1, step 2, step 3 + visual for each
PROOF (45-55s):
CTA (last 5s): one only
CAPTION: hook line + 1-2 sentences + question + 3-5 hashtags
```

**Longer video (3-8 min):** hook (15 s), problem, step-by-step demo in chapters, mistakes, result, next video suggestion.

**AI for scripting:** use AI to outline and tighten, then add your own results and opinions. Never post a script that is the same as everyone else's with a new tool name.

