## 8. Editing and quality

1. Cut silence and filler; keep it tight.
2. Burn in captions (many people watch with sound off); keep them in the center safe area.
3. Zoom or highlight what the viewer must see on screen.
4. Add quiet licensed music, voice louder than music.
5. Add a progress cue (step 1, 2, 3) so viewers stay.
6. Check on a phone before export.

**Export:** MP4, H.264, 1080x1920 (9:16), 30 fps, AAC audio. Check the current maximum Reel length in the uploader; a 30-90 second range is a good start. Longer Reels can hold more ad slots, but only lengthen when the content needs it.

**Quality checklist**
- [ ] Hook in the first 3 seconds
- [ ] Text readable on a small phone
- [ ] Clear voice
- [ ] No unlicensed music or other people's clips
- [ ] Facts verified from official sources
- [ ] Realistic AI media labeled where applicable
- [ ] No watermarks from other apps (a TikTok watermark can reduce reach)

